A||||10||eastex87gt||Where can I buy a model of my car???||||5||
Z||000000||eastex87gt||08-13-2001||10:49 PM||||I have a red and silver 87 gt and trying to find either a model or die cast of this car.  Any ideas??||||reg||5
Z||000001||ferg||08-13-2001||11:16 PM||||As far as I know, there is only one 86-88 die-cast Fiero- It was an Ertl Blueprint series- (1/43 scale). I believe it only came in one color- burgundy w/ silver trim.<P>I don't think there were any 1/24 or 1/18 scale die-casts made.<P>Micro Machine's came out w/ a few- I've seen pictures of some, but have never seen them in person. There are a few on the board who have them, maybe they will post a pic.<P>As for models, the 85 GT's are currently being made, and the only fastback Fiero's were made by (I think) MPC, they were discontinued a long time ago. This model comes up for sale from time to time on ebay.<P>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||08-13-2001||11:24 PM||||e-bay has models come up for sale all the time.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-14-2001||11:07 AM||||If you want a nice model of an 87 GT, I'm afraid you'll have to build it yourself.  ferg and Jay are right...eBay is the best place to find Fiero models.  Though I did get lucky by placing a classified ad in Scale Auto Enthusiast...got 5 notchback models for $40!<P>The blue 87 I built here is from MPC's 1/25 fastback GT.  It is actually an 86 (tranny is the 4-sp Muncie) but nobody knows the difference unless you tell them (oops!).<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20000815-1-001010.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20000815-1-001010.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||qwikgta||08-14-2001||11:47 AM||||You can always drill out the rivit on the bottom of a matchbox fiero, (they are all over ebay) and paint to match, thats what I did for my coupe.   Little diff for the GT crowd, no matchbox that I know of.  Also on ebay are many 1/24 or 1/25 scale models, GT and coupe both.  They go for about $25-40 each, I have bought a few as well.<P>Good luck<P>ROb||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-14-2001||11:51 AM||||HotWheels Did a FieroGT Fastback, I have one. BUT it is a giant 4x4 with machine guns sticking out the windows... maybe a new conversion?  I'll see if I can find it at home and take a pic.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero_24||08-14-2001||12:26 PM||||I just bought an 84 coupe, 85 GT, and an 87 GT off ebay.  I am building them.  I only paid $28 for the GT new in the box.  My Gt will go on my dash at shows and be painted to match.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||08-14-2001||12:36 PM||||I also have the '87 GT MPC/Ertl Model.  I've made the paint supply list, and have a spray can of the base paint from my car- planning on doing the same- miniture car on the dash (or engine?) for shows!||||reg||1
